[A-1] What is the primary endpoint of the study?
-----------------------------------------------------------------
{
    "result": {
        "response": "The study has two primary endpoints:\n\n## 1. Primary Efficacy Endpoint\n**Clinical and endoscopic remission at Week 12**, defined as:\n- Full Mayo score \u2264 2\n- No individual subscore > 1\n- Rectal bleeding subscore = 0\n\nThis is a binary outcome (remission status = yes/no) analyzed by a **logistic regression model** with treatment and randomisation-stratification factors (prior corticosteroids treatment and consent to participate in PK substudy) as fixed effects, and baseline full Mayo score as a covariate. Patients with missing remission status data are assumed to be **not in remission**. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 68)\n\nThe full Mayo score ranges from 0\u201312 (higher score = worse) and is based on clinician scoring of clinical signs/symptoms as well as endoscopic scoring of gross colonic mucosal inflammation. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 30)\n\n## 2. Primary Safety Endpoint\n- **Adverse events, vital signs, 12-lead Electrocardiography (ECG), and clinical safety laboratory abnormalities** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 7)",
