{
    "result": {
        "response": "The investigational medicinal product (IMP) in this trial is **TJ301 (FE 999301, Olamkicept [proposed INN])**, a solution for injection with the following composition: **15 mg/mL in solution [25 mM histidine, 200 mM sucrose, 0.1 mg/mL Polysorbate 20 in aqueous solution]** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 12).\n\nThe placebo is the same solution (25 mM histidine, 200 mM sucrose, 0.1 mg/mL Polysorbate 20 in aqueous solution) **without TJ301** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 12).\n\nKey administration details:\n- **Storage:** -20 \u00b1 5 \u00b0C, thawed at site by personnel blinded to randomisation\n- **Dilution:** 250 mL 5% (w/v) glucose\n- **Infusion time:** 2 hours\n- **Treatment arms:** Placebo (0 mg/mL TJ301), 300 mg (1.03 mg/mL TJ301), and 600 mg (2.07 mg/mL TJ301), all with a total infusion volume of 290 mL (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 12).\n\nThe IMP is also identified on the title page as **TJ301 (solution for injection), also referred to as FE 999301 and Olamkicept**, for the indication of **Active Ulcerative Colitis** in a Phase II study (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 1).",
