    "result": {
        "response": "## Randomisation Stratification\n\nIn this study, randomisation is stratified by **two factors**:\n\n1. **Prior corticosteroids treatment** (yes/no)\n2. **Consent to participate in PK substudy** (yes/no)\n\n(Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 36; p. 26; p. 8)\n\nThis information is collected at **Visit 1** and used at **Visit 2** for randomisation by stratification based on these factors. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 36)\n\n> **Note:** These stratification factors replaced the original criteria used in protocol Version 1.0, which had stratified by *elevated CRP levels (\u22653 mg/L)* and *stable conventional treatment (prior treatment with amino salicylates, corticosteroids, and immunosuppressive drugs)*. The current factors were introduced in **Version 1.1** of the protocol. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 92)",
