[A-12] How is the study drug stored and prepared?
-----------------------------------------------------------------
{
    "result": {
        "response": "## Study Drug Storage and Preparation\n\n### Storage Conditions\nBoth **TJ301** and **placebo** must be stored at **-20 \u00b1 5\u00b0C** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.39; p.40; p.12).\n\n### Thawing & Preparation\n- Both IMP vials are **thawed at the pharmacy/site** by site personnel who are **blind to study randomisation** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.39; p.12).\n- After thawing, the IMP is **diluted in 250 mL 5% (w/v) glucose** for infusion (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.39; p.40; p.12).\n- The specific concentrations after dilution are:\n  - **300 mg group:** 1.03 mg/mL TJ301\n  - **600 mg group:** 2.07 mg/mL TJ301\n  - **Placebo group:** 0 mg/mL TJ301\n  (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.39)\n\n### Post-Reconstitution Storage\nOnce reconstituted and diluted for infusion, the IMPs should be **stored at 15\u201325\u00b0C** and **used as soon as possible within 3 hours of preparation** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.40).\n\n### Administration\n- **Route:** Intravenous (IV) infusion (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.39)\n- **Infusion volume:** 290 mL (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.40)\n- **Infusion time:** 2 hours (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.40; p.39; p.12)\n- **Schedule:** Every 2 weeks for 12 weeks (6 infusions in total) (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.40)\n\n### Post-Infusion Monitoring\n- After the **1st and 2nd infusions**: patients are monitored for infusion reactions for **3 hours** post-infusion (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.40).\n- After **remaining infusions**: patients are monitored for **1 hour** post-infusion (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.40).",
        "sources": [
