    "result": {
        "response": "## Key Inclusion Criteria for TJ301 Clinical Trial (Active Ulcerative Colitis)\n\nA subject will be eligible for inclusion in this study only if **all** of the following criteria apply:\n\n1. **Age:** Male and female patients 18\u201370 (inclusive) years of age. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 34)\n\n2. **Confirmed Active UC:** Active UC confirmed by colonoscopy with biopsy or flexible sigmoidoscopy with biopsy at Screening, with extending >15 cm past the anal verge from endoscopy. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 34)\n\n3. **Disease Severity:** Active UC with a full Mayo score \u22655 and a rectal bleeding subscore \u22651 at screening. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 34)\n\n4. **Endoscopy Subscore:** During Day \u221235 to Day \u22126 prior to Randomisation, an endoscopy subscore \u22652. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 34)\n\n5. **Prior Conventional Therapy:** Treated with conventional non-biological UC therapy:\n   - Corticosteroids stable for at least 2 weeks prior to Randomization at no more than 20 mg prednisone (or equivalent), **and/or**\n   - 5-aminosalicylates (5-ASA) at no less than 2 g/day for at least 3 months and stable for at least 4 weeks prior to Randomization, **and/or**\n   - Azathioprine (AZA) at no less than 1.5 mg/kg/day or mercaptopurine (6-MP) at no less than 0.75 mg/kg/day for at least 6 months and stable for at least 6 weeks prior to Randomization. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 34)\n\n6. **Contraception/Fertility:** A female subject has been sterilized or has been menopausal, or the subject has no pregnancy plan during the trial and voluntarily adopts effective contraceptive measures. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 34)\n\n7. **Protocol Compliance:** The patient is able and willing to comply with the requirements of this trial protocol. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 34)\n\n8. **Literacy:** The subject should be able to read and write to understand and fill out Patient Diary. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 34)\n\n9. **Informed Consent:** Voluntarily signed Informed Consent obtained before any trial-related procedures are performed. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 34)",
