        "response": "## Assessments at Week 12 (Visit 8 \u2013 End of Treatment)\n\nThe following assessments are performed at the Week 12 End of Treatment (EoT) visit:\n\n### Disease Activity & Efficacy\n- **Full Mayo Score** (complete, including endoscopic subscore) (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.50)\n- **Endoscopy** (sigmoidoscopy or colonoscopy) (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.9; p.26)\n- **Mucosal biopsies** for assessment of mucosal healing, histology, and immunohistochemistry \u2014 collected during endoscopy (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.9; p.26)\n- **9-point partial Mayo Score** (also collected at all treatment visits) (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.50)\n\n### Laboratory & Sampling\n- **Blood sampling for PK assessments** (all visits, including Visit 8) (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.50)\n- **Faeces sampling for calprotectin** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.50)\n- **Blood sampling for exploratory biomarkers** \u2014 must be taken when the patient is in a fasting state (\u22658 hours) (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.50)\n- **Clinical laboratory tests** (blood and urine sampling) (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.50)\n- **Urine pregnancy test** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.50)\n- **Blood sampling for anti-TJ301 antibodies** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.50)\n\n### Physical & Safety Assessments\n- **Physical examination** (body weight only) (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.50)\n- **Vital signs** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.50)\n- **12-lead ECG** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.50)\n\n### Administrative\n- **Diary review** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.50)\n- **Concomitant medications documented** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.50)\n- **Adverse events documented** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.50)\n\n> **Note:** Diary dispensing is only performed at Visits 3\u20137 and therefore does **not** occur at Visit 8. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.50)",
