        "response": "The question 'What are the requirements?' is broad and could refer to different sets of criteria in the document. Based on the available context, the most relevant requirements are the **Inclusion Criteria** for patient eligibility in the TJ301 ulcerative colitis clinical trial. All 9 inclusion criteria are listed below:\n\n---\n\n## Inclusion Criteria \u2013 TJ301 Ulcerative Colitis Trial\n\nA subject will be eligible for inclusion in this study only if **all** of the following criteria apply:\n\n1. **Age:** Male and female patients **18\u201370 (inclusive)** years of age. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 9)\n\n2. **Disease Confirmation:** Active UC confirmed by colonoscopy with biopsy or flexible sigmoidoscopy with biopsy at Screening, with extending **> 15-cm** past the anal verge from endoscopy. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 9)\n\n3. **Disease Severity:** Active UC with a **full Mayo score \u2265 5** and a **rectal bleeding subscore \u2265 1** at screening. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 9)\n\n4. **Endoscopy Subscore:** During Day -35 to Day -6 prior to Randomisation, an **endoscopy subscore \u2265 2**. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 9)\n\n5. **Prior Conventional Non-Biological UC Therapy:** Treated with at least one of the following:\n   - Corticosteroids stable for **at least 2 weeks** prior to Randomization at **no more than 20 mg prednisone** (or equivalent), and/or\n   - 5-aminosalicylates (5-ASA) at **no less than 2 g/day** for **at least 3 months** and stable for **at least 4 weeks** prior to Randomization, and/or\n   - Azathioprine (AZA) at **no less than 1.5 mg/kg/day** or mercaptopurine (6-MP) at **no less than 0.75 mg/kg/day** for **at least 6 months** and stable for **at least 6 weeks** prior to Randomization.\n   (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 10)\n\n6. **Contraception:** A female subject has been sterilized or has been menopausal, or the subject has no pregnancy plan during the trial and voluntarily adopts effective contraceptive measures. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 10)\n\n7. **Protocol Compliance:** The patient is able and willing to comply with the requirements of this trial protocol. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 10)\n\n8. **Literacy:** The subject should be able to read and write to understand and fill out Patient Diary. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 10)\n\n9. **Informed Consent:** Voluntarily signed Informed Consent obtained before any trial-related procedures are performed. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 10)\n\n---\n\n> **Note:** If you were asking about a different set of requirements (e.g., exclusion criteria, dosing requirements, or procedural requirements), please clarify and I can provide a more targeted answer.",
